WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.060
Speaker 1: All right.

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:03.290
I have a couple of quick stories to briefly
talk about.

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:04.460
This is an interesting one.

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:09.230
It is now appearing that Donald Trump has
been desperate to appear on Joe Rogan's podcast

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:10.810
and that Joe Rogan has turned him down.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:14.320
We're going to look at a clip of Rogan himself
explaining this.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.940
There's a Daily Beast article.

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:20.910
Joe Rogan reveals he's rejected Trump multiple
times for interview.

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:23.949
Rogan recently declared his support for Ron
DeSantis.

00:00:23.949 --> 00:00:29.970
On Tuesday, he said he's absolutely no Trump
fan and has no desire to assist them in any

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:32.410
way, shape or form.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.540
This was on a podcast with host Lex Friedman,
and Rogan talked about how weird the Trump

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.530
era is going to be in retrospect.

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:45.530
Some of the reasons Rogan cited are not ones
I agree with.

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:46.530
But that's okay.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:51.470
Let's listen to what Joe Joe Rogan had to
say about Trump wanting to be on his show.

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:55.350
Speaker 2: By the way, I'm not a Trump supporter
in any way, shape or form.

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:58.140
I've had the opportunity to have on my show
more than once.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.710
I've said no every time and I want to help
him.

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:02.080
I'm not interested in helping now.

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:09.409
Speaker 1: One interesting question is whether
such an interview would be a good interview

00:01:09.409 --> 00:01:12.049
for someone like Joe Rogan and his show.

00:01:12.049 --> 00:01:18.749
Because when you think about the Rogan format,
which is three hour conversations and I've

00:01:18.749 --> 00:01:27.799
been on for two of them on his show, often
in depth and sort of flighty.

00:01:27.799 --> 00:01:30.990
Non sequential thinking.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.810
Is not very conducive to those types of conversations.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:35.450
And this is what Trump does.

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:39.049
You ask him about one thing and you say, Hey,
you know what?

00:01:39.049 --> 00:01:40.829
What's the deal with you?

00:01:40.829 --> 00:01:42.340
I heard you like fast food.

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:45.759
Yeah, well, you know, KFC, you know, they
make it.

00:01:45.759 --> 00:01:47.469
They make a tremendous bird.

00:01:47.469 --> 00:01:52.109
And but the thing is, you know, the Democrats
and radical Joe Biden, they want to control

00:01:52.109 --> 00:01:53.109
everything.

00:01:53.109 --> 00:01:54.990
Not only did he lose, he wants to take away
burgers.

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:57.210
And I mean, we just you just can't have it.

00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:58.290
And I said I would fix it.

00:01:58.290 --> 00:01:59.290
I would fix all of it.

00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:00.389
I would fix trade.

00:02:00.389 --> 00:02:05.029
You know, it's it's not he's not even really
able to have that type of a conversation.

00:02:05.029 --> 00:02:10.119
And, you know, the speculation of Trump with
adult ADHD or whatever, I think the guy just

00:02:10.119 --> 00:02:13.950
has no idea what's going on in any serious
depth with any topic.

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:15.660
I think that's really the explanation.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:20.830
And Trump would ramble on and interrupt and
interject about the election stolen or whatever.

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:27.891
So from like a conversational standpoint,
I don't know how Trump does a three hour conversation

00:02:27.891 --> 00:02:28.891
with Rogan.

00:02:28.891 --> 00:02:32.150
That's not a praise or a criticism of the
format.

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:33.940
I think it's a great thing.

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:37.340
It's great to have podcasts of all different
formats, and the three hour conversation is

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:39.870
a great format for people who can do it.

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:44.159
It doesn't seem to me that that Trump could
do it now in terms of Rogan doesn't want to

00:02:44.159 --> 00:02:52.800
help Trump, as I've said before, I don't think
there is any like big mystery about Rogan.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:03:00.151
I think Rogan admits he's not the most keyed
into politics and Rogan, to a degree, is a

00:03:00.151 --> 00:03:01.590
chameleon of sorts.

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:08.640
When I was on his show and I espoused all
of my left wing ideas, Joe agreed with almost

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:10.629
everything I had to say.

00:03:10.629 --> 00:03:17.129
And then when he has on, you know, whoever
from the right, he agrees generally with most

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:18.129
of the things they have to say.

00:03:18.129 --> 00:03:23.430
He's had disagreements that I've covered with
people, like he's had disagreements with Ben

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:25.400
SHAPIRO on some things.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:29.330
He's had disagreements with Candace Owens,
you know, right wingers in a sense.

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:38.060
And to a degree, I think that what's happening
with Rogan is he is, um, when it comes to

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:43.180
a lot of different areas, he is clearly on
the left when you get into the details.

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:45.300
I think he genuinely is.

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:48.930
I think he's also culturally conservative.

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:56.069
A lot of the circles he's now in, you know,
UFC and Dana White, definite right wing bent

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:57.069
there.

00:03:57.069 --> 00:04:01.790
He's now in Texas and reportedly, I think
has a relationship with the governor there,

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:04.709
Greg Abbott, who's an extreme right winger.

00:04:04.709 --> 00:04:09.620
He's in this environment where there's a lot
of kind of de facto right wing thinking.

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:12.400
And then like on DeSantis, I just think he's
sort of confused.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:18.970
I don't even think Rogan is aware that DeSantis
stands for the opposite of most of the things

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:21.190
Rogan has espoused support for.

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:26.770
So I don't think we need to get into this
thing of like ascribing a significant morality

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:27.770
to it.

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:34.470
I think politics isn't Rogan's main thing,
and he finds common ground with almost anyone

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:36.009
he talks to.

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:42.520
And while he is socially liberal to a great
degree, he's also in a culturally conservative

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:44.590
environment and that rubs off on him.

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:50.860
So interesting for sure how much we glean
from it about anything in particular other

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:56.060
than Trump's desperation to get on Rogan's
podcast, which is interesting, is probably

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:57.100
not to too much

